--- !u!114 &522777376
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 522777374}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3ff6acaa8b9f1994499dd387e6188532, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Comments: "This scene demonstrates several ways material shader properties may
    be animated using Timeflow.\n\nTimeflow - Set Shader Time is enabled which sets
    the time value to the global shader property named \"_TimeflowTime\". All custom
    shader graphs that use this property can perform time-based interpolations without
    any added animation setup in the scene. This is used in lieu of the built-in
    Time node in Shader Graph.\n\nBeatInfluence - sends channel value to a global
    shader property named \"_Beat01\" which affects all shaders with the property.\n\nGlobal
    Shader Properties\nShader properties may have any name you wish as long as it
    is globally unique. Also be sure that any shader properties you wish to target
    globally are not exposed in Shader Graph (ie the Exposed checkbox is off). Otherwise
    the property will not receive the value.\n\nMaterial Instancing\nWhenever using
    Timeflow behaviors to animate material properties, it only affects the single
    material. If the material is shared among multiple objects, in edit mode it will
    appear all objects are updating with the same changes to the material. However,
    at runtime Unity creates material instances which are no longer shared, only
    affecting the single object it is applied to. \n"
  Warning: It is important to understand instancine behavior when animating material
    properties directly. Using global shader properties is a way to overcome material
    instancing and optimize material animations so that all materials using the same
    shader receive the animation changes. Otherwise, each object will need to replicate
    the material animation, or linked using channel link.
  URLTitle: Shader Properties Documentation
  URL: https://axongenesis.gitbook.io/timeflow/reference/examples/shader-properties
  URL2Title: 
  URL2: 
